// QUIC frames, RFC 9000 §19:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9000#section-19
//
// What a packet's payload is made of: CRYPTO, STREAM, ACK, the flow-control
// frames, the connection-close frames and the rest. Bytes in, a frame out.
//
// The ACK frame's range encoding is here too (§19.3.1), both directions: a receiver's
// record of which packet numbers arrived, and the set an ACK's fields describe.
//
// Which frames a packet may carry, and what to do with one, is the connection's
// business and not this package's.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moonvar/quic",
}
